error[E0277]: `&'static str` cannot be shared through a Duet store
 --> tests/ui/borrowed.rs:8:12
  |
8 |     label: &'static str,
  |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^ no `SharedState` impl exists for `&'static str`
  |
  = help: the trait `SharedState` is not implemented for `&'static str`
  = note: Duet refuses a type by not implementing `SharedState` for it. The usual fixes:
            `u64` `u128` `i128` `usize` `isize`  ->  `i64` (the wire's only integer is `i64`; `u64 > i64::MAX` has no representation)
            `f32`                                ->  `f64` (Dart and TS have no 32-bit float, so `f32` is lossy inbound for nothing)
            `HashSet<T>`                         ->  `Vec<T>` or `BTreeSet` via a hand impl (hash order is not a function of the value)
            `HashMap<K, V>` with `K` != `String` ->  `HashMap<String, V>` (`Value::Map` has string keys; a list of pairs loses path addressing)
            `Vec<u8>` as binary                  ->  `duet::Bytes` (a bare `Vec<u8>` is accepted, but lowers to a list of ints)
            `&str` `&[T]` and other borrows      ->  the owned type (the store owns a `'static` tree)
            `Rc` `RefCell` `Cell` `Mutex` `RwLock` -> the inner type (two handles to one node become two copies through `Value`)
            `PathBuf` `OsString`                 ->  `String` (`OsString` is WTF-8 on Windows; `Value::Str` is UTF-8 only)
            `Duration` `SystemTime` `Instant`    ->  an explicit `i64` or `String` encoding you choose
            `Option<Option<T>>`                  ->  `Option<T>` (`Some(None)` and `None` both lower to `Value::Null`)
          For anything else, write `impl SharedState for &'static str` yourself — it is a supported escape hatch, not a workaround.
